# rantai-kb (Rust) dev stack — copy to .env and edit.
#
#   cp rust/deploy/.env.example rust/deploy/.env
#
# Docker Compose reads this file automatically because it sits next to
# compose.yaml; anything exported in your shell wins over it. Every setting here
# is optional: without a .env the stack runs with the defaults shown (the
# commented value is the default). Nothing in this file is a real secret; the
# credentials are the local dev ones from rust/scripts/stack-up.sh.
#
# Two rules worth knowing:
#   * A variable that is PRESENT wins over the KB_TIER preset, even when empty.
#     `KB_CACHE_DIR=` therefore means "no disk cache", not "use the default".
#   * Changing tiers with existing data is not supported: lite/lite-en embed at
#     384 dimensions, everything else at 1024. Run `rust/scripts/kb-dev.sh down -v`
#     before switching between those two classes.

# ─── Host ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Host port for kb-server. Change it if 8080 is taken; stores publish nothing.
KB_PORT=8080

# Ports/hostnames are otherwise fixed by the compose network; kb-server always
# listens on 8080 inside its container.

# ─── Build ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Cargo parallelism for the image build. 2 keeps a shared dev machine usable;
# unset uses all cores.
# CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2

# Tag for the built image (all six tiers share one image).
# KB_IMAGE_TAG=dev

# Reported by GET /health so you can tell which build is running.
# KB_VERSION=dev

# ─── Dev store credentials (local only, not secrets) ────────────────────────

# POSTGRES_USER=kb
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=kb
# POSTGRES_DB=rantai_kb

# rustfs (S3) credentials; it reads these as MINIO_ROOT_USER/PASSWORD.
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=kbadmin
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=kbsecret123
# S3_BUCKET=rantai-kb
# S3_REGION=us-east-1

# ─── Models and inference ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

# One embedder or two (0.4.0, `DEP-6`). Desk, Studio and Station only.
#
# Unset (the default) keeps two models: Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B for text and
# Qwen3-VL-Embedding-* for page images. `one` embeds both with
# Nemotron-3.5-Embed-1B in a single 2048-d space and reranks with
# Qwen3-Reranker-0.6B — measured at text 0.826 vs 0.796, pages 0.621 vs 0.277,
# reranker +0.055, and 1.19 GB of reranker instead of 4.26/17.5 GB
# (docs/eval-ab/one-embedder/, docs/eval-ab/rerank-2026-11-17/).
#
# It needs a vLLM `/v2/embed` endpoint (the preset points at
# http://127.0.0.1:8081/v2/embed; compose passes the service name) and a
# llama.cpp or TEI `/v1/rerank` at :8082. Adopting it is a RE-INDEX, not a config
# change: text vectors go 1024 -> 2048 and Qdrant fixes a collection's width at
# creation (docs/rust-cutover.md §17).
# KB_EMBEDDERS=one

# Local tiers only (lite, lite-en, desk, studio, station): the tier preset points
# these at loopback, which is wrong inside compose, so compose.yaml substitutes
# the service hostname. Setting them here wins over that substitution — use it to
# run the models on another machine instead of in this stack.
#
# An OpenAI-compatible embedding server (llama.cpp `llama-server --embedding`,
# vLLM, another TEI) and a reranker:
#
#   KB_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.20:8081/v1/embeddings
#   KB_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=local
#   KB_RERANK_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.20:8082/v1/rerank
#   KB_RERANK_PROVIDER=cohere
#
# KB_RERANK_PROVIDER=cohere is what llama.cpp's /v1/rerank takes (the Cohere
# request shape) and KB_RERANK_BASE_URL is then the full endpoint. For another
# TEI, keep KB_RERANK_PROVIDER=tei and give the base URL without /rerank.
# KB_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://tei-lite:80/v1/embeddings
# KB_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=local-tei
# KB_RERANK_PROVIDER=tei
# KB_RERANK_BASE_URL=http://tei-rerank-desk:80

# CPU budget for the lite/lite-en embedder and kb-server. The measured 2-core
# numbers (docs/eval-ab/lite-2core) had both sharing the same 2 cores; embedding
# is ~95% of ingest, so more embedder CPUs = faster ingest. Keep KB_EMBED_THREADS
# equal to KB_LITE_EMBED_CPUS.
# KB_LITE_EMBED_CPUS=2.0
# KB_LITE_SERVER_CPUS=2.0
# KB_EMBED_THREADS=2

# Local OCR for scanned pages and image uploads. The tier preset fills these
# (Lite: the CPU document sidecar ./ocr-cpu; Desk and up: Xiaomi-OCR-0 on vLLM,
# recipe `xiaomi`); set one here only to override it. `rantai-kb setup` writes
# them for you: `--ocr mistral` (hosted), `--ocr <url>` (a shared OCR server),
# `--ocr off`. An EMPTY KB_OCR_BASE_URL means "no local OCR server".
# KB_OCR_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions
# KB_OCR_MODEL=xiaomi-research/Xiaomi-OCR-0
# KB_OCR_RECIPE=xiaomi        # or paddle: the CPU sidecar and other text-only servers
# KB_OCR_API_KEY=
# KB_OCR_DPI=150              # Lite preset: 110
# KB_OCR_CONCURRENCY=16       # Lite 2, Desk 16, Studio/Station 32
# Mistral OCR instead (hosted, billed per page): empty KB_OCR_BASE_URL plus
# KB_MISTRAL_OCR_KEY=
# KB_LAYOUT_EXTRACTOR_ORDER=mistral

# Xiaomi table pass (`setup --ocr-tables accurate`): the PP-DocLayoutV3 sidecar
# on the CPU (never on the vLLM GPU). Requests queue behind it, hence the timeout.
# KB_OCR_LAYOUT_URL=http://ocr-layout:8193
# KB_OCR_LAYOUT_TIMEOUT_MS=900000
# KB_OCR_LAYOUT_CPUS=4.0

# TEI image for the GPU tiers. The plain tag is CUDA; use :<ver>-turing for
# Turing-class cards, or a rocm- tag for AMD.
# TEI_GPU_IMAGE=ghcr.io/huggingface/text-embeddings-inference:1.8.1

# vLLM (OCR on every GPU tier; studio/station: page embedder, reranker).
# First start downloads several GB of weights; raise KB_WAIT_SECONDS (kb-dev.sh
# `up`, default 900) to 1800 or more on a slow link.
# VLLM_IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai:v0.32.0
# VLLM_OCR_IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai:v0.33.0   # Xiaomi-OCR-0 was measured on this one
# LLAMA_CPP_CUDA_IMAGE=ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp:server-cuda
# HF_TOKEN=
# Xiaomi-OCR-0 per GPU tier: pages in flight, the fixed KV cache, and the share
# of the card the process may use (it peaked at 4.4 GB with 16 pages / 1 GiB).
# KB_DESK_OCR_SEQS=16
# KB_DESK_OCR_KV_BYTES=1073741824
# KB_DESK_OCR_GPU_FRACTION=0.45
# KB_STUDIO_OCR_SEQS=32
# KB_STUDIO_OCR_KV_BYTES=2147483648
# KB_STATION_OCR_SEQS=32
# KB_STATION_OCR_KV_BYTES=2147483648
# Share of the whole GPU each vLLM container claims (estimates, not measured).
# KB_STUDIO_OCR_GPU_FRACTION=0.2
# KB_STUDIO_PAGE_EMBED_GPU_FRACTION=0.2
# KB_STUDIO_RERANK_GPU_FRACTION=0.2
# KB_STATION_OCR_GPU_FRACTION=0.12
# KB_STATION_PAGE_EMBED_GPU_FRACTION=0.2
# KB_STATION_RERANK_GPU_FRACTION=0.2
# CPU document OCR sidecar on lite/lite-en (scanned pages only): layout +
# PP-OCRv6 tiny + SLANet-plus tables. `text` mode skips layout and tables.
# KB_LITE_OCR_CPUS=2.0
# KB_LITE_OCR_WORKERS=2
# KB_OCR_THREADS=2
# KB_LITE_OCR_MODE=structure
# KB_LITE_LAYOUT_MODEL=pp_layout_cdla   # yolov8n_layout_general6 is faster but its
#                                       # licence needs an application to 360 for
#                                       # commercial use (docs/model-licences.md)

# ─── Spend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Cloud only (paid). `kb-dev.sh up cloud` refuses to start without it.
# Get one at https://openrouter.ai/keys — do not commit the value.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ─── Ingest / retrieval extras (all off by default, all free) ───────────────

# Local tiers keep entity extraction off and use the heuristic extractor, so a
# stray OpenRouter key is never spent by an ingest. Set both to turn the graph on:
#   KB_ENTITY_EXTRACTION_ENABLED=true
#   KB_ENTITY_EXTRACTOR=heuristic   # or llm to pay OpenRouter
#   KB_GRAPH_STORE=pg
#   KB_GRAPH_ARM=true
# KB_ENTITY_EXTRACTION_ENABLED=false
# KB_ENTITY_EXTRACTOR=heuristic
# KB_GRAPH_STORE=none
# KB_GRAPH_ARM=false

# Content-addressed embedding/extraction cache inside the container. It lives on
# the kb-cache volume and survives `down` (not `down -v`). Set it empty to disable
# caching — every ingest then pays for its embeddings again.
# KB_CACHE_DIR=/app/cache

# Log level for the server (`RUST_LOG` syntax).
# RUST_LOG=info
